---
alwaysApply: true
---
- Always use TypeScript (`.ts` and `.tsx` files) instead of JavaScript.
- Prefer functional components over class components.
- Follow clean code principles: readability, reusability, minimal side effects.
- Always include proper types for props, state, and function returns.
- Never use `any` unless absolutely unavoidable — use generics or utility types instead.
- Keep imports organized: React/Next first, third-party libraries second, local files last.
- Use named exports unless a file exports a single React component.
- Use `const` for constants and `let` only when reassignment is required.
- In case on conflict instructions in AGENTS.md takes prefernce.
- Keep docs and code in sync